{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp1", "text": "Intention is the leader of things; intention is first, they’re made by intention. If with corrupt intent you speak or act, suffering follows you, like a wheel, the ox’s foot.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp1", "chapter": "1. Pairs", "tone": "harsh", "topics": ["decline"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 30, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "doom", "selection": "tone=- topic=['decline', 'death'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp15", "text": "Here they grieve, hereafter they grieve, an evildoer grieves in both places. They grieve and fret, seeing their own corrupt deeds.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp15", "chapter": "1. Pairs", "tone": "harsh", "topics": ["decline"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 21, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "doom", "selection": "tone=- topic=['decline', 'death'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp114", "text": "Better to live a single day seeing the state free of death than to live a hundred years blind to the state free of death.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp114", "chapter": "8. The Thousands", "tone": "neutral", "topics": ["death"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 25, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "doom", "selection": "tone=- topic=['decline', 'death'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp128", "text": "Not in midair, nor mid-ocean, nor hiding in a mountain cleft; you’ll find no place on the planet where you won’t be vanquished by death.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp128", "chapter": "9. Wickedness", "tone": "neutral", "topics": ["death"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 25, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "doom", "selection": "tone=- topic=['decline', 'death'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp129", "text": "All tremble at the rod, all fear death. Treating others like oneself, neither kill nor incite to kill.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp129", "chapter": "10. The Rod", "tone": "harsh", "topics": ["death"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 18, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "doom", "selection": "tone=- topic=['decline', 'death'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp131", "text": "Creatures love happiness, so if you harm them with a stick in search of your own happiness, after death you won’t find happiness.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp131", "chapter": "10. The Rod", "tone": "neutral", "topics": ["death"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 23, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "doom", "selection": "tone=- topic=['decline', 'death'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp132", "text": "Creatures love happiness, so if you don’t harm them with a stick in search of your own happiness, after death you will find happiness.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp132", "chapter": "10. The Rod", "tone": "stern", "topics": ["death"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 24, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "doom", "selection": "tone=- topic=['decline', 'death'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp135", "text": "As a cowherd drives the cows to pasture with the rod, so too old age and death drive life from living beings.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp135", "chapter": "10. The Rod", "tone": "neutral", "topics": ["death"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 22, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "doom", "selection": "tone=- topic=['decline', 'death'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp148", "text": "This body is decrepit and frail, a nest of disease. This foul carcass falls apart, for life ends in death.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp148", "chapter": "11. Old Age", "tone": "neutral", "topics": ["death"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 20, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "doom", "selection": "tone=- topic=['decline', 'death'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp150", "text": "In this city built of bones, plastered with flesh and blood, old age and death are stashed away, along with conceit and contempt.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp150", "chapter": "11. Old Age", "tone": "neutral", "topics": ["death"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 23, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "doom", "selection": "tone=- topic=['decline', 'death'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp158", "text": "The astute would avoid being corrupted by first grounding themselves in what is suitable, and then instructing others.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp158", "chapter": "12. The Self", "tone": "harsh", "topics": ["decline"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 18, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "doom", "selection": "tone=- topic=['decline', 'death'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp165", "text": "For it is by oneself that evil’s done, one is corrupted by oneself. It’s by oneself that evil’s not done, one is purified by oneself. Purity and impurity are personal matters, no one can purify another.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp165", "chapter": "12. The Self", "tone": "harsh", "topics": ["decline"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 36, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "doom", "selection": "tone=- topic=['decline', 'death'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp170", "text": "Look upon the world as a bubble or a mirage, then the King of Death won’t see you.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp170", "chapter": "13. The World", "tone": "neutral", "topics": ["death"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 18, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "doom", "selection": "tone=- topic=['decline', 'death'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp21", "text": "Heedfulness is the state free of death; heedlessness is the state of death. The heedful do not die, while the heedless are like the dead.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp21", "chapter": "2. Diligence", "tone": "stern", "topics": ["death"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 25, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "doom", "selection": "tone=- topic=['decline', 'death'] (curation, not generation)"}
